Description:

Sieve scripts that use the "ihave" extension (RFC 5463) are now compiled
more strictly.  An extension becomes usable only once it is named in
"require" or after a successful "ihave" test on it, and then only for the
remainder of the script.  Syntax errors are suppressed only inside the block
guarded by a failed "ihave" test.  Previously any "ihave" test made every
extension usable, and a failed test suppressed syntax errors elsewhere in
the script too, which let an otherwise-rejected script run and read
uninitialized stack memory into its variables.


